194139533814 true] [17592186253115 1034 "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253115 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253115 1111 #uuid "39f37ba1-7389-55d1-bf28-49281e0e8906" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253116 1034 "A={\\int }_{-1}^{3}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253116 1111 #uuid "eae215c7-3278-5d4b-8e49-bebe4be46528" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253117 1034 "A={\\int }_{-3}^{0}(-{x}^{2}+2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253117 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253117 1111 #uuid "67bde883-eb69-5a08-b447-620c886549d5" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253118 1034 "A={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-{x}^{2}+2x-2)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253118 1111 #uuid "b6323d20-174b-5e5e-8caa-d3eb68eb2af3" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253119 1034 "A={\\int }_{-3}^{0}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253119 1111 #uuid "42a33424-33f8-581b-83a4-b211b10c281e" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253120 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253121 13194139533814 true] [17592186253120 1089 "q-315830" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253120 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533814 true] [17592186253120 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{4}9{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}9{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[9($\n{{field-1}}\n$)^{\\,3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]$" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253120 1113 #uuid "5ba8ef0d-4afc-57f3-a6e1-978f702b493c" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253120 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}9{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=9{x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=1$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}9{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(1+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(1+\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[9{(1+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{\\,3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253121 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253122 13194139533814 true] [17592186253121 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533814 true] [17592186253121 1041 "field-1" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253121 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253122 13194139533814 true] [17592186253121 1110 #uuid "82711246-7818-567e-acca-65c5baf0326d" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253122 1034 "1+\\frac{3i}{n}" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253122 1111 #uuid "cf514bb4-ecac-5d78-a01e-f1fa6b00f140" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253124 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253127 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1089 "q-346180" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1100 "Find the function $f(x)$ and the value of $b,$ given that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[({2}^{\\,2+3k/n}+1)\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and \n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1113 #uuid "088d1080-7491-5e6a-87a2-5180d45dc341" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253123 1145 "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=2.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{3}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{n}=\\frac{b-2}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=5.\n$$\n\nConsequently, ${x}_{k}=2+\\frac{3k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})={2}^{\\,{x}_{k}}+1.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{5}({2}^{x}+1)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[({2}^{\\,2+3k/n}+1)\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \n\n$$\nf(x)={2}^{x}+1\\,\\text{and}\\,b=5.\n$$" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253125 13194139533814 true] [17592186253124 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253126 13194139533814 true] [17592186253124 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533814 true] [17592186253124 1041 "field-1" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253124 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253126 13194139533814 true] [17592186253124 1110 #uuid "f085c8ab-d5da-55c2-b14f-64548a810098" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253125 1034 "2^x-1" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253125 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253125 1111 #uuid "d10c97e6-7ea4-5522-8feb-1d49481b5656" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253126 1034 "2^x+1" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253126 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253126 1111 #uuid "1fb83b21-9c07-50dc-ae3b-faa6b4be20c0" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253128 13194139533814 true] [17592186253127 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533814 true] [17592186253127 1041 "field-2" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253127 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253128 13194139533814 true] [17592186253127 1110 #uuid "9749fad5-d5c5-57bf-af31-496187f79966" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253128 1034 "5" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253128 1111 #uuid "aba5708e-7651-5cf7-ad88-1fb8cca73e9f" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253129 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253130 13194139533814 true] [17592186253129 1089 "q-346217" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253129 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533814 true] [17592186253129 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a right Riemann sum?\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]$" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253129 1113 #uuid "cf543ae6-1922-5af8-939a-ac9fd71c7458" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253129 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a right Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\sqrt{x+1},$ the lower bound is $a=0$ and the upper bound is $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\sqrt{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(0+i\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{3i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\sqrt{(\\frac{3i}{n})+1}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}[\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{3i}{n}+1}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253131 13194139533814 true] [17592186253130 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533814 true] [17592186253130 1041 "field-1" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253130 1104 #edb/ref 17592186253131 13194139533814 true] [17592186253130 1110 #uuid "1775c1a2-f343-5dea-be06-9959b482b353" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253131 1034 "\\sqrt{\\frac{3i}{n}+1}" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533814 true] [17592186253131 1111 #uuid "9e1bd4e8-308d-5c6c-956b-c26f5db48a9f" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253132 1017 #edb/ref 17592186253133 13194139533814 true] [17592186253132 1089 "q-49188" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253132 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533814 true] [17592186253132 1100 "What is ${\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253132 1113 #uuid "fd742197-ec3d-517e-9c40-387f07be0a49" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253132 1145 "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{3},$ the lower bound is $a=2,$ and the upper bound is $b=6.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{6-2}{n}=\\frac{4}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{6}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(2+\\frac{4i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{4i}{n})}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533814 true] [17592186253133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253134 13194139533814 true] [17592186253133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253135 13194139533814 true] [17592186253133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253136 13194139533814 true] [17592186253133 1000 #edb/ref 17592186253137 13194139533814 true] [1759218625313